# The base problems of the family repeated_reduction_mixin_builtin_natural: the check
# C.Equal(A.Plus(B)) of MIXINv2's Builtin NatPlusZero, NatPlusSuccessor,
# NatEqualityZero and NatEqualitySuccessor, a numeral n written as n
# Successor objects over Zero as MIXINv2/packages/mixinv2-library/tests/NatConstants.mixin.yaml
# writes them, read at church. A sum that fails is off by one.
#
# THE SNAPSHOT of each is the Boolean of the equation, computed with integers.
# PROOF: plus and equality descend on the predecessors of finite numerals,
# each class with one implementation of each member read.
#
#   natural_point(?Point, ?Left, ?Right, ?Result)
#
# Each text is from_cbor of a string literal, a Scott list of bytes,
# imported from corpora/library/text/cbor. Each number is from_cbor of an
# integer literal, a Scott integer, imported from corpora/library/integer/cbor.
# FIXME: the imports project "corpora" https://github.com/Atry/private-overlay/issues/1923
# off the variable gezi, the name of the project root's own
# directory; it breaks if that directory is renamed.
